Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:58:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/31] v3d: fewer threads when a TMU request exceeds the
 per-thread FIFO

Cube/array shadow lookups with bias or LOD write five values; with four
threads each thread has four FIFO slots. Reduce threads until
next_coord <= 16 / threads. Fixes six GPU resets in shadow cases.
---
 src/broadcom/compiler/v3d33_tex.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/broadcom/compiler/v3d33_tex.c b/src/broadcom/compiler/v3d33_tex.c
index b4c888a..31dfd5d 100644
--- a/src/broadcom/compiler/v3d33_tex.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/compiler/v3d33_tex.c
@@ -170,6 +170,12 @@ v3d33_vir_emit_tex(struct v3d_compile *c, nir_tex_instr *instr)
                 vir_get_uniform_index(c, QUNIFORM_TEXTURE_CONFIG_P1, p1_packed),
         };
 
+        /* The TMU input FIFO has 16 slots shared by all shader threads.
+         * A cube/array shadow lookup with LOD or bias needs five writes.
+         */
+        while (next_coord > 16 / c->threads)
+                c->threads /= 2;
+
         for (int i = 0; i < next_coord; i++) {
                 struct qreg dst;
 
